        "original_id": "46e51906-7552-55f9-8900-79c27609e417",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Billy Nungesser, Kip Holden, John Bel Edwards, David Vitter, Bill Cassidy\n- Events: Louisiana lieutenant gubernatorial election, 2015; Louisiana gubernatorial election, 2015\n- Roles: Lieutenant Governor of Louisiana, Governor of Louisiana, United States Senator for Louisiana\n\nFacts:\n- David Vitter was born on May 3, 1961.\n- In 2005, David Vitter began serving as a United States Senator for Louisiana.\n- In the 2015 Louisiana lieutenant gubernatorial election, Billy Nungesser defeated Kip Holden.\n- In the 2015 Louisiana gubernatorial election, John Bel Edwards defeated David Vitter by a similar margin despite the Democratic victory occurring in a different statewide race.\n- In 2017, David Vitter ended his service as a United States Senator for Louisiana and retired.\n- In 2017, Bill Cassidy became Louisiana's senior senator after David Vitter retired.\n- David Vitter is an American lobbyist, lawyer, and politician.",
